# A typed table made with a search function keeps a search index, and
# Table.search(words) gives the rows whose search text holds every word,
# whole and caseless, that the table's row policy lets the caller read. A
# put replaces a row's words and a delete removes them. The same lines
# print at O0, O1 and O2.
fixture: SearchIndexMatchesEveryWordUnderPolicy.fixture
env: NO_COLOR=1
step default: jet run main.jet
exit: 0
stdout: = search_index_matches_every_word_under_policy.stdout.expected
step: jet build main.jet
exit: 0
step debug: built
exit: 0
stdout: == default
step release: jet run --release main.jet
exit: 0
stdout: == default
